{"hash": "9c46d94d1a704387", "text": "A coding agent is a head cook sending in helpers. Every command it runs is its own child process, so a dev server it starts belongs to the agent. Long commands go to the background. In Claude Code, slash tasks lists them, and it says it cleans them up when it exits. Not every tool does. What's new is fences: sandboxes limiting what its commands and their children can touch. As of this month, Claude Code's sandbox covers Mac, Linux and W S L two, not native Windows. Codex's Windows sandbox also stops leftover child processes. And Microsoft's Execution Containers, a way to fence agents in on Windows, became generally available this month. Some agents use them already; others say they will. Task Manager's Isolation column shows only the fences built on Windows' app containers. Vendors are moving toward agents as their own kind of process, with their own account.", "alignment": {"characters": ["A", " ", "c", "o", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", "g", "e", "n", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "a", " ", "h", "e", "a", "d", " ", "c", "o", "o", "k", " ", "s", "e", "n", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "n", " ", "h", "e", "l", "p", "e", "r", "s", ".", " ", "E", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "c", "o", "m", "m", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "t", " ", "r", "u", "n", "s", " ", "i", "s", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "o", "w", "n", " ", "c", "h", "i", "l", "d", " ", "p", "r", "o", "c", "e", "s", "s", ",", " ", "s", "o", " ", "a", " ", "d", "e", "v", " ", "s", "e", "r", "v", "e", "r", " ", "i", "t", " ", "s", "t", "a", "r", "t", "s", " ", "b", "e", "l", "o", "n", "g", "s", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "a", "g", "e", "n", "t", ".", " ", "L", "o", "n", "g", " ", "c", "o", "m", "m", "a", "n", "d", "s", " ", "g", "o", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", "g", "r", "o", "u", "n", "d", ".", " ", "I", "n", " ", "C", "l", "a", "u", "d", "e", " ", "C", "o", "d", "e", ",", " ", "s", "l", "a", "s", "h", " ", "t", "a", "s", "k", "s", " ", "l", "i",